; TLDR: ADDITIONAL INFO TO MAP REACTIVE GROUPS FROM T to T*

; .fgroup
; Functional group definitions
; refers to abstract functional groups, so a functional group alone
; defines what type of reactivity it can do

; the main goal of these files is to manage how molecules with functional
; groups are loaded into memory

; this is a work in progress, the comments are based on imagination

; A "functional group"
[ fgroup ]
MOLNAME

; atoms involved in the functional group
; rid is how they are numbered in reaction templates
; role is whether it is "init", "norm" or "edge"

; init is the initiator atom, used for distance cutoffs in templates
; norm are atoms part of the functional group
; edge are atoms not part of the functional group

; there must be exactly one initiator atom per functional group

; edge atoms can be used for reaction condition constraints
; or to create or destroy angles/dihedrals with, as long as they 
; aren't a center atom in the angles/dihedrals created/destroyed

; bonds involving edge atoms, angles centered on edge atoms or dihedrals
; centered on edge atoms can be assumed to not be modified during reactions

; bonds only involving only init or norm atoms, angles centered on init or norm
; atoms and dihedrals centered on init or norm atoms exclusively should
; be listed as "reactive" forces in this example ritp, to load them in
; memory in an order consistent for the same functional group, regardless
; of what itp is used.

; any atoms bonded to any init or norm atom in any form (any shared angle,
; bond, dihedral) should be included as an edge atom at least

[ atoms ]
; rid role
   1  init
#ifdef EDGE
   2  edge
   3  edge
   4  edge
#else
   ; just a test of #ifdefs
   2 norm
   3 norm
   4 norm
#endif

; internally, T* should construct a list of *reactive forces*:
; list of all bonds involving only init or norm atoms
; list of all angles centered on init or norm atoms
; list of all dihedrals centered exclusively on init or norm atoms
; (so edge-init-norm-edge belongs here but edge-init-edge-norm 
; for example doesn't)
; all these bonds will be deleted when a reaction happens and need to
; be replaced from the product itp

; Input molecules (input topologies) might contain molecules that have this
; functional group, list which ones and map the id's to rid's. Have some
; sanity checks that they are mapped correctly - match types, atom names too
; title keyword is fmap.molname
[ fmap ]
BDT
[ atoms ]
; rid    id(in itp)    type   name
   1         1          TC6    S1
   2         2          TC6    S2
   3         3          TC5    C3
   4         4          TC5    C4
; can have multiple fmap's to have multiple possible itp's with the same fg
